# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.

# The backend's URL. Leave blank to fall back to Vite's same-origin dev
# proxy (see vite.config.ts's proxy block) — set explicitly when the
# backend needs to be reached directly (a different port than the proxy
# targets, a remote/staging backend, etc.). Setting this requires the
# backend's SERVER_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS to include this frontend's own
# origin (http://localhost:3000 by default) — otherwise every request gets
# silently blocked by the browser's CORS policy with no visible error
# beyond the browser console (see the "Can't reach the backend" banner,
# src/components/common/BackendStatusBanner.tsx, for the user-facing side
# of that failure mode).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8085
